# Student display name

When **showing or composing** a student name for lists, cards, menus, exports, notifications, search labels, or API `name` / `studentName` fields, use:

**first + second + family** (`firstName` / `first_name_*` + `secondName` / `secondNameEn` + `lastName` / `last_name_*`).

## Rules

- Prefer the shared helpers: frontend `formatStudentDisplayName` (`utils/student-display-name.ts`), backend `formatStudentDisplayName` (`common/identity/bilingual-name.ts`).
- Do **not** use only `firstName` + `lastName` (drops the second name).
- Do **not** include `thirdName` / `thirdNameEn` in the short display string. Third name stays on the record and on full legal/register forms (all four parts), not in list/label display.
- Skip empty parts; join with a single space.
- Locale: prefer Arabic parts when the UI is Arabic, English parts when English; fall back to the other language, then legacy `firstName` / `secondName` / `lastName`.

## Anti-pattern

```ts
// BAD
`${student.firstName} ${student.lastName}`

// GOOD
formatStudentDisplayName(student)
```
